; The one real UP-Term drawer as UPTREAL: (a multi-directory UP-Term: writes to its first directory only):
; the drawer ENVARC:up-term/Dir names when it exists, else UP-Term:'s own first directory. The single source of
; this lookup: resolve-addon.dos includes it, and an add-on's launch icons, skills and data deletes include it
; alone. Sets $uptmoved to YES when UPTREAL: was pointed at the Dir drawer. The caller drops the assign.
Assign >NIL: UPTREAL: UP-Term:
Unset uptmoved
If EXISTS ENVARC:up-term/Dir
  Set uptdir "`Type ENVARC:up-term/Dir`"
  ; Assign of a missing drawer returns 20, which stops a script whose FailAt is lower: look first.
  ; An empty Dir file leaves $uptdir empty, and EXISTS "" asks for a volume: skip it then
  If NOT "$uptdir" EQ ""
    If EXISTS "$uptdir"
      Assign >NIL: UPTREAL: "$uptdir"
      If NOT WARN
        Set uptmoved YES
      EndIf
    Else
      Echo "[WARN] ENVARC:up-term/Dir names $uptdir, which does not exist: installing into UP-Term: itself."
    EndIf
  EndIf
EndIf
